>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / What Is Sports Psychology?</p>
      <h1>What Is Sports Psychology?</h1>
      <p>Sports psychology is the study of how psychological factors affect athletic performance, and how participation in sport affects a person's mental state.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="page-body">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p>Sports psychologists work with athletes, coaches, and teams to build mental skills such as focus, confidence, motivation, and composure under pressure. The field covers practical techniques like visualization, self-talk, goal setting, and pre-performance routines, alongside the study of topics like team dynamics and performance anxiety.</p>
      <p>This page is the starting point of our full guide. Our in-depth articles on <a href="/mental-skills/">mental skills</a>, <a href="/degrees/">degrees</a>, and <a href="/careers/">careers</a> build on the foundations introduced here.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
